<p>Absolutely incredible. I love the idea. +1. But to be helpful, I have two small criticisms:<br />
&quot;SCP-3268 also varies heavily in size, usually depending on the device it is taking a residence in at the moment. The smallest recorded sighting being approximately 0.5 millimeters in diameter, and the largest being 5 meters in diameter&quot;<br />
This wording is confusing, but I am assuming you mean that the image does not matter, it will generally have the same amount of pixels when spawned?<br />
Also, I would put footnotes for the scientific name of those animals which have the common name in them. I don't want to have to search for each scientific animal name to know which animal it is talking about.<br />
Other than that, this was on point and very good of an idea. Great job!</p>

